-- Two review repairs pinned by this corpus (2026-08-16):
--
-- 1. The stored field `alternative` collides with a DAObject method name
--    (`suitable alternative accommodation` is live legal vocabulary — see
--    the Housing Act Sch.2 corpus). The emitter must keep generated
--    attributes out of the DAObject class/instance namespace (here it emits
--    `o.alternative_`): plain `o.alternative` finds the truthy bound method,
--    __getattr__ never raises, docassemble never backchains to the question,
--    and the interview returns a silent wrong verdict.
--
-- 2. The computed (MEANS) field `meets the minimum` is stripped from the
--    record by the desugarer, which synthesizes a top-level selector decide
--    in its place; the projection onto it must inline that selector — the
--    pre-repair emitter refused with the false diagnostic
--    "record `Offer` has no field `meets the minimum`".

DECLARE Offer
    HAS
      @desc Whether suitable alternative accommodation is on offer
      `alternative`       IS A BOOLEAN
      @desc Annual salary offered, in dollars
      `salary offered`    IS A NUMBER
      `meets the minimum` IS A BOOLEAN MEANS `salary offered` AT LEAST 3000

@export Whether the offer is lawful
GIVEN o IS AN Offer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offer lawful` o IF
    o's `meets the minimum` AND NOT o's `alternative`

-- The method-shadow detector: with the pre-repair emission, `alternative`
-- is never asked and rides in truthy, forcing the goal FALSE — so this
-- TRUE case catches the shadow.
#EVAL `offer lawful` OF
        Offer
        WITH
            `alternative`    IS FALSE
            `salary offered` IS 3500
-- TRUE

#EVAL `offer lawful` OF
        Offer
        WITH
            `alternative`    IS TRUE
            `salary offered` IS 3500
-- FALSE

-- Below the minimum: short-circuit prunes the `alternative` question.
#EVAL `offer lawful` OF
        Offer
        WITH
            `alternative`    IS FALSE
            `salary offered` IS 2000
-- FALSE
